      "mechanism_card": {
        "hypothesis": "R0's traversal-tail dots (the last 5% of the parent's own FIFO-BFS selection order) still carry unique kernel credit on short late-visited strands, so removing them lowers DTI slightly rather than releasing false-positive mass.",
        "mechanism": "DTI = T / (0.2T + 0.2(S-M) + 0.8|G|). Dropping a dot removes 1 from S (helping the 0.2(S-M) term) but deletes its max-kernel credit wherever it was the best coverer of a truth pixel (hurting T). The parent's recorded recipe ranks its dots by 8-connected FIFO-BFS traversal of the H19-5 support; the dropped tranche is the lowest-priority tail (visit ranks 114510-121128 of 0-121128, n=1,883 of 37,654).",
        "non_fault_confounder": "FIFO-BFS order is a raster convention (seeds at the first raster pixel of each 8-connected support component), not geological confidence: tail dots are the far ends of long lineaments and late chips, where drainage divides and lithologic contacts mimic fault strands. The local report-only PROXYs lean the same sign (catalogue hide-and-recover delta -0.0003; SGMC control delta -0.008), but SGMC-mapped faults are not the new-fault truth and neither PROXY is a score.",
        "predicted_live_change": "-0.002 DTI (MODEL; plausible interval -0.010 to +0.003; not a score)",
        "falsifier": "Paired same-week receipt vs R0: delta >= +0.010 confirms the false-positive regime and re-opens the sibling -10/-20% rungs; delta <= -0.010 shows the tail carries unique fault credit and closes the drop direction. |delta| < 0.010 is no evidence under the session rule.",
        "structural_geologist_note": "Read this as a dose rung on the lineage's own selection order, not as a claim that fault traces end where the traversal ends. Inspect the dropped SE ends and small chips on geology before any slot is spent."
      },
